id: pm-0jzl5t
title: "Release verification shares the build job's timeout and waits fifteen minutes while npm's publish-time scan can hold a version longer: 2026.11.8 was published but the job was cancelled before acceptance"
description: "## Observed\nOn 2026-11-08 the blocker-retry Auto Release run 42451940007 cut tag v2026.11.8. Its tag-push Release run 42454411958 published @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.8 at 07:11:28Z: npm printed \"+ @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.8\" and \"Your package is being processed and may take a few minutes to become available\".\n\nThe registry still answered E404 for the exact version at 07:31Z. The \"Verify published package on npm, npx, and bunx\" step had polled 59 of its 60 attempts when the \"Build, Test, Publish\" job hit its 60-minute timeout at 07:26Z and was cancelled. The pre-publish stages took 45 minutes that day (the coverage gate alone took 24 minutes, against 14 minutes on 2026-11-07), so the verify step got only 15 of its declared 20 minutes.\n\nRegistry acceptance and GitHub Release advertisement were skipped, and npm latest stayed at 2026.11.7. The auto-release run recorded release-workflow as its failing stage on blocker issue 1686.\n\n## Cause\n1. npm now scans every new version for malware at publish time, before the version becomes installable (GitHub changelog 2026-07-28). The scan typically takes about five minutes, and \"up to 15 minutes or more\" at peak times or depending on content and size. 2026.11.7 became visible 5m12s after publish (04:39:25Z to 04:44:37Z); 2026.11.8 took longer than 20 minutes. pm-wzmbvn fitted the 60-poll ceiling to the 6-8 minute propagation lag measured in 2026-09.\n2. The verify step runs in the same job as build, tests and gates. Its wait budget is therefore whatever the job timeout leaves after a pre-publish phase of variable length, and nothing guarantees it the 20 minutes its step timeout declares.\n3. Recovery is expensive. Re-running the failed job repeats 45 minutes of build, test and gates before it reaches a version that is already published.\n\n## Fix direction\n- Move post-publish verification into its own publication job that needs the release job and has its own timeout. That covers the npm/npx/bunx verifier, the installed agent sessions and the previous-release control selection.\n- Raise the default npm metadata wait to about thirty minutes.\n- Make the failure text name npm's publish-time scan and the cheap recovery: re-run only the failed publication job.\n- Re-budget the Auto Release parent for the extra serial job, using the reserve formula from pm-29bwud.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No change to npm publish, trusted publishing or the immutable-tag rules.\n- No retry of npm publish; publication was correct."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
