acceptance_criteria: "release.yml runs the npm/npx/bunx verifier, the installed agent sessions and the previous-release control selection in a separate publication job that needs the release job, checks out the exact published source and owns the version and previous outputs; installed-acceptance and advertise depend on it; verify-published-release.mjs defaults to at least 240 npm metadata polls (at least sixty minutes, above the 55m22s hold measured for 2026.11.8), its usage states the default, and a unit spec proves the default without --npm-attempts; An npm metadata failure names the exact version, the elapsed poll budget, npm's publish-time scan and the recovery that re-runs only the failed publication job; a unit spec asserts the text; The ci-workflow contract spec pins the publication job budget and keeps the Auto Release parent at or above the sum of the serial child limits plus the reserves and below the 360-minute hosted job limit; docs/RELEASING.md describes the job split and the recovery; The next scheduled cut passes the publication job on attempt 1 or fails for a cause other than npm metadata visibility, recorded on pm-e70zh5"
parent: pm-wzmbvn
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "release.yml moves the npm/npx/bunx verifier, installed agent sessions and previous-release control into a publication job (110-minute limit, verify step 95) that checks out the release job's recorded published source and that installed-acceptance and advertise depend on; verify-published-release.mjs defaults to 360 polls (about ninety minutes) and an exhausted wait names the version, npm's publish-time scan and gh run rerun <run-id> --failed; auto-release parent 290 minutes; contract specs pin the budgets"
expected_result: "A correct publication held by npm's scan for up to ninety minutes passes verification without manual help, and a longer hold is recovered by re-running only the publication job"
actual_result: "Contract specs pin the publication job, its step budgets and the parent formula; negative controls fail against the previous workflow and default; the next scheduled cut is recorded on pm-e70zh5"
